tion or intravenous immunization with <italic>Candida albicans</italic></article-title><source><italic>Journal of Infectious Diseases</italic></source><year>1994</year><volume>170</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>390</fpage><lpage>395</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8035025</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Na</surname><given-names>B-K</given-names></name><name><surname>Song</surname><given-names>C-Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of monoclonal antibody in diagnosis of candidiasis caused by <italic>Candida albicans</italic>: detection of circulating aspartyl proteinase antigen</article-title><source><italic>Clinical and Diagnostic Laboratory Immunology</italic></source><year>1999</year><volume>6</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>924</fpage><lpage>929</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10548587</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Su</surname><given-names>Q-P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>G-Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Production of hybrid phage displaying secreted aspartyl proteinase epitope of <italic>Candida albicans</italic> and its application for the diagnosis of disseminated candidiasis</article-title><source><italic>Mycoses</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>50</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>171</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17472610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Angiolella</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Facchin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Stringaro</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><